2026-09-27T10:28:05.0451956Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0452234Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0452656Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0453142Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0453307Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0453634Z ================
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0453828Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0454042Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0454631Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0455001Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0455187Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0455637Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0455922Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0456140Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0456766Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0457356Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0458687Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0459615Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0459790Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0460516Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0461568Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0462032Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0462535Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0463232Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0463411Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0463725Z ========
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0463896Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0466147Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0469365Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0469723Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0470570Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0471763Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0472762Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0553782Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0554566Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0555303Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0555454Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0555825Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0556038Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0557696Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0562144Z 
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0563187Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0564489Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:28:05.0564801Z 
